{
  "about": "THE PRESS-RISK WORDS — ONE list of word roots that make a button (or a command) sound like money, deleting, resetting or the account. The kit ENFORCES it at every gated press (PressGuard.RiskyRoot — PressGuardSharedCasesTests.cs) and in CheatRisk; the website reads the SAME roots: the tick list's risk (renderer tick-list.ts riskyRootOf), the reader's DESTRUCTIVE? mark (renderer lane-digest.ts soundsDestructive: destructiveRoots only), and the near-name rule, which never offers a risky name as a one-press fix (apps/api press-risk.ts, near-name.ts). Each side keeps its constants in code and its spec holds them EQUAL to this file, so the copies cannot drift. Words split at non-letters and camelCase humps; a root matches the START of a word; 'log out' / 'sign out' read as one word in every spelling. Revive_Gems_Button has no risky ROOT: the near-name rule refuses it by its own spend-noun rule (near-name.cases.json), not by this list.",
